{
  "instrument": "violin",
  "description": "Pressing a button holds down ALL FOUR strings at once, N semitones above each string's own open pitch -- it is a full-row action, not a per-string one. 'buttons' below is the primary/authoritative table: button number -> the exact 4-note row it produces (this is what the physical controller does). 'notes' is a DERIVED reverse index (pitch name -> canonical button+string) built from that table, for looking up what button to chart for a given target pitch. Because one button produces 4 pitches at once, and some pitches are reachable via more than one row-position (adjacent strings overlap by a note at the position boundary), 'notes' just records ONE canonical choice per pitch (preferring the lowest button number / open strings) plus any runner-up(s) in 'alternatives' -- it does not change what the hardware actually does, which is always press the whole row.",
  "switch_count": 7,
  "bow_direction_rule": "alternate",
